---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';

const toc = [
	{ id: 'acceptance', label: 'Acceptance' },
	{ id: 'educational-use', label: 'Educational use' },
	{ id: 'no-advice', label: 'No professional advice' },
	{ id: 'estimates', label: 'Estimates and accuracy' },
	{ id: 'your-responsibilities', label: 'Your responsibilities' },
	{ id: 'intellectual-property', label: 'Intellectual property' },
	{ id: 'third-parties', label: 'Third-party links and ads' },
	{ id: 'warranties', label: 'Disclaimer of warranties' },
	{ id: 'liability', label: 'Limitation of liability' },
	{ id: 'indemnity', label: 'Indemnity' },
	{ id: 'governing-law', label: 'Governing law' },
	{ id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
	{ id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<LegalPage
	title="Terms of Use | NetHourly"
	description="Terms for using NetHourly's free pay, overtime, 24-hour shift, and hourly wage calculators. Estimates are educational, not payroll, legal, tax, or financial advice."
	eyebrow="Terms · estimates · limitations"
	heading="Terms of use."
	lede="NetHourly is a free educational calculator. By using it, you agree to these terms. The numbers are estimates, not a paycheck, a legal opinion, or tax advice."
	updated="October 27, 2026"
	breadcrumbLabel="Terms of Use"
	toc={toc}
>
	<h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance of these terms</h2>
	<p>
		These terms apply to NetHourly.com and its calculators, guides, and pages. By using the
		site, you agree to these terms and to the{' '}
		<a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>. If you do not agree, do not use the site.
	</p>

	<h2 id="educational-use">Educational use only</h2>
	<p>
		NetHourly provides general educational tools for understanding US pay periods, overtime,
		24-hour shift pay, and hourly wages. The site is not a payroll service, employer,
		staffing agency, law firm, accounting firm, tax preparer, or financial adviser. It is not
		affiliated with the US Department of Labor, any state labor agency, or any employer.
	</p>
	<p>
		You are responsible for checking your own pay stub, employment agreement, union contract,
		and applicable law. A calculator result is a starting point for a conversation, not a
		final determination of what you are owed.
	</p>

	<h2 id="no-advice">No payroll, legal, tax, or financial advice</h2>
	<p>
		Nothing on NetHourly is payroll, legal, tax, investment, or financial advice. The site
		does not create an attorney-client, accountant-client, or fiduciary relationship. Wage
		and hour law is fact-specific and changes over time. Overtime eligibility, sleep and
		meal exclusions, daily overtime, and tax withholding depend on your duties, location,
		employment agreement, and other facts.
	</p>
	<div class="legal-note">
		<p>
			<strong>For a real dispute, get real help.</strong> Confirm current rules with the US
			Department of Labor, your state labor office, a union representative, or a qualified
			payroll, tax, or legal professional. Do not rely on this site to decide whether to file
			a claim, sign a contract, or accept a settlement.
		</p>
	</div>

	<h2 id="estimates">Estimates and accuracy</h2>
	<p>
		The calculators use simplified assumptions: a 40-hour week, 52 weeks a year, 26
		bi-weekly pay periods, FLSA overtime after 40 hours, and flat-rate tax estimates. Real
		payroll may differ because of state and local taxes, pre-tax deductions, garnishments,
		credits, filing status, overtime rules, holiday pay, bonuses, shift differentials, or
		unpaid time off.
	</p>
	<p>
		We aim to keep formulas and reference data accurate, but we do not guarantee that every
		figure is current, complete, or error-free. Minimum wages, tax rates, and overtime rules
		change. If you spot an error, contact us with the page and the number in question.
	</p>

	<h2 id="your-responsibilities">Your responsibilities</h2>
	<p>When using NetHourly, you agree not to:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Use the site for unlawful, fraudulent, or harmful purposes.</li>
		<li>Attempt to disrupt, overload, or gain unauthorized access to the site.</li>
		<li>Scrape, copy, or republish substantial portions of the site without permission.</li>
		<li>Misrepresent calculator results as official payroll, legal, or tax determinations.</li>
		<li>Submit sensitive personal information such as Social Security or bank account numbers.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		You are responsible for the accuracy of the numbers you enter and for how you use the
		results. The calculators do not verify your hours, rate, classification, or eligibility.
	</p>

	<h2 id="intellectual-property">Intellectual property</h2>
	<p>
		The site's text, design, layout, calculators, and original graphics are owned by
		NetHourly or used with permission. You may view the site and print a page for personal,
		non-commercial use. You may not copy, modify, distribute, sell, or create derivative works
